    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the email-uniqueness rule for owner creation, following the existing duplicate-detection patterns already in the codebase (telephone, household, city).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`DuplicateEmailException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` in the `rest.advice` package, mirroring `DuplicateTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DuplicateEmailException` that returns **409 Conflict** with an `errors` array naming the `email` field, consistent with the other duplicate handlers.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `rejectDuplicateEmail(...)` guard and wired it into `addOwner`. The check:\n   - Runs on the normalized (lower-cased) email produced by the existing `normalizeEmail`.\n   - Compares case-insensitively against every existing owner's email (each stored value is lower-cased before comparison), so `Jane@Example.com` collides with `jane@example.com`.\n   - Skips the check when no email is supplied (`null`), matching the fact that email is optional.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` passes: creating a second owner with an already-used email now returns 409.",
